'' THE STANDARD PACKAGE (ADR 0017; RFC-0007 §5-6; RFC-0009): 'std/strings' and 'std/fs' from
'' the toolchain's pkg/ -- found beside the compiler, as <exe-dir>/../pkg in the repository.
'' Both are facades over fb/ headers, found through -i as a user's toolchain finds them in
'' its inc/: Split returns an Array( of string ), Repeat takes the count first, and fs keeps
'' std/path's names for the header's functions -- so '/x' is not absolute on Windows, and
'' 'C:\x' is.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc -i toolchains/tiko-windows/inc tests/modules/src/stduse/main.bas -o tests/modules/stdlink.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' RUN: tests/modules/stdlink.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT:  4 abc
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: true          true          false
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: a+b+c ababab
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: okit 007
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: c.txt .txt a/b
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: false true a\b
